      "title": "Australia news live: police locate parents of toddler found wandering Sydney street alone at 2am",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/01/nepal-tibet-flooding-missing-australians-penny-wong-anthony-albanese-pacific-islands-forum-liberal-national-coalition-one-nation-politics-reactions-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow updates live</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>43 Australians still missing, with concerns growing ‘every day, every hour’ that goes by, Wong says</strong></p><p>The foreign affairs minister, <strong>Penny Wong, </strong>says there are still 43 Australian missing after the flooding in Nepal, saying the government holds grave concerns for their safety that only gets worse as the days go by.</p><p>This is such a distressing time and I know this is so difficult for the family and friends of those 43 Australians.</p><p>Every day, every hour, only increases our concern for those who have not been found and remain missing, and that is many Australians. … You can imagine how many families and friends are traumatised as a consequence.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/01/nepal-tibet-flooding-missing-australians-penny-wong-anthony-albanese-pacific-islands-forum-liberal-national-coalition-one-nation-politics-reactions-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-01T02:00:04"
    },
    {
      "title": "Man shot and killed in Sydney home invasion was ‘targeted attack’, police believe",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/01/man-shot-killed-glen-alpine-sydney-home-invasion-nsw-police-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Alleged offenders at large after man in his early 20s fatally shot in early hours of Tuesday</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/01/nepal-tibet-flooding-missing-australians-penny-wong-anthony-albanese-pacific-islands-forum-liberal-national-coalition-one-nation-politics-reactions-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A man in his early 20s has been fatally shot in an alleged home invasion in Sydney’s south-west that police believe was a “targeted attack”. A homicide investigation is under way, with the alleged offenders still at large.</p><p>Acting Supt Gretchin Atkins said the man, who was yet to be formally identified, was at his Glen Alpine home with his family in the early hours of Tuesday morning when multiple individuals allegedly broke in.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/01/man-shot-killed-glen-alpine-sydney-home-invasion-nsw-police-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-01T00:09:59"
    },
